{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>He does</b>: This is the blessing—that he knows with faith of the heart that HaShem does righteous deeds, and that He is righteous in all His ways. And the meaning of this: because he mentioned afflictions, he mentioned HaShem with justice and faith toward him. And behold, he stated that He will execute justice if a man distorts a straight path and is chastised with suffering—and this is one who is obligated to his Creator; likewise, to creatures like himself he will execute judgment. Therefore: <i>and justice for all the oppressed</i>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 103, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:58.466804689Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}